  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 315 PM EDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\n- Multiple Rounds of Showers and Thunderstorms, Warm and Humid\n\nWe remain on the northern edge of a heat dome and in a \"ring of\nfire\" pattern around the SE CONUS high through at least Wednesday.\nPredictability has been fairly low in this pattern, with varied\nmodel solutions regarding thunderstorm development, as so far the\nlast few days the storms have been based on weak ripples in the \nmid and upper-level flow and moisture advection at 800-700 mb.\nStorms this afternoon are likely not to be surface based, and\ndowndraft CAPE is also meager, but they could mix down some 30 mph\ngusts locally.\n\nHeat advisories were considered mainly for near I-94 as NBM highs\nin the lower 90s and dew points in the lower 70s Tuesday and \nWednesday may push the heat index above 100. However, uncertainty \nin cloud cover and thunderstorm potential leans us toward holding \noff for now.\n\nThunderstorm potential is very iffy on Tuesday and most models are\nnot enthusiastic in convective development. A plume of higher CAPE\nand adequate deep-layer shear overhead on Tuesday does support a\nmarginal risk of severe winds or hail if isolated thunderstorms do\ndevelop. It's possible for surface-based storms to develop over\nMid/Central Michigan later in the day, or for an upstream complex\nto cross Lake Michigan, per a few models. But confidence is low,\nand ended up broadbrushing 20-30 percent chances for precip over \nmuch of the area.\n\nA somewhat more pronounced shortwave may eject out of the western\nCONUS and could lead to more thunderstorms, perhaps an MCS, at\nsome time during the day Wednesday, with another marginal or\nslight risk for severe winds or hail.\n\nDespite the worst of the heat getting nudged south by an \namplifying ridge/trough pattern over the Central to Northeast US \nafter Wednesday, the majority of ECE members have been retaining \nMUCAPE over the area through at least Thursday and Friday. The 12z\ndeterministic ECMWF has not been nearly as amplified with the\nridge/trough also. This may support additional chances for\nelevated thunderstorms later in the week, more so favored over\nsouthwest Michigan.",
